From c29b3f9f0b1dedf4e55722212f4272b9eabb6b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:18:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1022/1178] Remaster: the Debunker v6 pipeline on a take or its
 stems

HERESY 1022. Post has Remaster. heresy-lab runs the Debunker v6 (lab/debunker.py,
the HERETICAL TANDEM post-processing pipeline) on the take itself or on one of
its stem sets: the Debunker mixes the stems with a preset (flat, balanced,
vocal forward, instrumental focus, shamanic) and per-stem levels from the page,
checks them for drift, then strips metadata, cleans up and fades, de-esses,
retunes to 432 Hz (off keeps 440 for the public), sets the loudness and exports.
With drums, bass and other present the instrumental stays out of the mix (it is
their sum). Each run is its own branch of the take's tree, with its settings
and the loudness measured in and out.
In the lab's copy the loudness step is two passes (measured, then a linear
gain) and keeps 48 kHz: one pass landed at -12.8 for -14 and, since ffmpeg's
loudnorm works at 192 kHz, wrote 192 kHz files four times the size.
The tree keeps watching a running job through dropped answers on a slow line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
